"damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"An unmanned enemy drone that has been upgraded from its namesake model, the Monster MkII. Equipped with a small gun and a long-range Arts receiver, they are likely operated by concealed Casters. Though unlikely to cause heavy damage to armored Operators, they can still pose a considerable threat.","abilities":["Flying unit."],"levelCount":2,"level":1,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.9,"stats":{"hp":2500,"atk":330,"def":125,"res":35,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":3}},"infused_glacial_originium_slug_enemy_1067_snslime_2":{"slug":"infused_glacial_originium_slug_enemy_1067_snslime_2","name":"Infused Glacial Originium Slug α","icon":"/enemies-icons/Infused Glacial Originium Slug α.webp","rank":"Normal","race":"Infected Creature","movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"An infected wild creature native to colder environments that has become unstable due to assimilating a large amount of Originium into its abdomen. More threatening than normal Infused Glacial Originium Slugs, they explode upon death, damaging and freezing nearby Operators. Due to their low intelligence, they are easily controlled by Yeti Squadron members for various tactical purposes.","abilities":["Upon death, deals Physical damage in an area and applies Cold to affected targets"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":1,"stats":{"hp":4850,"atk":370,"def":0,"res":0,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":1.7}},"airborne_soldier_leader":{"slug":"airborne_soldier_leader","name":"Airborne Soldier Leader","icon":"/enemies-icons/Airborne Soldier Leader.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"One of Reunion's special melee soldiers, more dangerous than a normal Airborne Soldier. They are equipped with modified disposable jetpacks made from looted parts. Despite their fairly rudimentary equipment, Reunion uses them to great effect when attacking insufficiently protected areas.","abilities":["Able to land directly onto the battlefield."],"levelCount":2,"level":1,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":1,"stats":{"hp":3000,"atk":400,"def":220,"res":20,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":1.9}},"yeti_operative":{"slug":"yeti_operative","name":"Yeti Operative","icon":"/enemies-icons/Yeti Operative.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A basic melee combatants of the Yeti Squadron hailing from teams of infected guerilla warriors in the Northwestern Tundra. They are skilled at attacking frozen Operators.","abilities":["Attack power increases when attacking Frozen targets"],"levelCount":2,"level":1,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":1.1,"stats":{"hp":5000,"atk":380,"def":135,"res":0,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2}},"oneiros":{"slug":"oneiros","name":"Oneiros","icon":"/enemies-icons/Oneiros.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Drone","movement":"Flying","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"An unmanned, slow-flying enemy drone equipped with a special warhead released upon approaching Operators that inflicts Arts damage and a freezing effect in an area. Modified from the Bombtail, they lost their ability to accelerate after delivering the payload in order to accomodate a special warhead.","abilities":["Flying unit.","Can launch a warhead to deal AoE Arts damage and apply the Cold effect to targets"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":4000,"atk":500,"def":180,"res":30,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":1}},"yeti_icecleaver_leader":{"slug":"yeti_icecleaver_leader","name":"Yeti Icecleaver Leader","icon":"/enemies-i